---
title: "And then…"
note: "Your own clip, going on forever, a little stranger every time. Wire a video into the Orrery Prompt's video input: the head speaks for it (its END ON: says how it ends, in words that fit any clip), and the first scene continues it, picture and sound (AFTER: the input video). Then every clip rolls what happens next, and everyone in it carries on as if nothing were odd, still marked by what happened the clip before ($event[-1]). Run (Instant) plays it until you stop. Orrery Continue needs the H3 video and audio VAEs in its vae and audio_vae."
tags: [loops, h3, reel, input_video, motion_context]
---
@h3 text 16:9
style: live-action, the same look, light and camera as the footage before it, one continuous shot
context: 22
MUSIC: N/A
END ON: the footage reaches its last moment, everything exactly where it was

@lib and_then
  a single red balloon drifts slowly through the frame
  it starts to snow, softly, indoors as much as out
  every loose object lifts a few centimetres off the ground and hangs there
  a brass band marches straight through the middle of the scene and out the other side
  the light turns to a deep golden sunset in a matter of seconds
  the walls fold away like stage flats, and behind them is a beach at noon
  a whale glides past in the sky, close enough to touch
  everything begins to move in slow motion except one small dog
  the colours drain out of the world one by one until only red is left
  a second, identical version of the scene slides in from the left and overlaps the first
  gravity tips sideways, and everyone leans into it calmly
  the camera's own reflection appears in the air, waving

SCENE and then
AFTER: the input video
$event = __and_then__
SHOT 6s: static
Everything carries on exactly where the footage left off, and then $event. Nobody seems to find it strange.
SFX: the footage's own sound carrying on; then the sound of what happens, close and clear
END ON: everyone settles back into what they were doing, as if nothing had happened

SCENE and then some forever
$event = __and_then__
SHOT 6s: static
The scene carries on, still marked by the moment $event[-1], and then $event. Everyone takes it in their stride.
SFX: the scene's sound carrying on; then the sound of what happens, close and clear
END ON: everyone settles back into what they were doing, as if nothing had happened
